What is LinkedList?

Definition:

LinkedList is a class in the Java Collection Framework that implements the List interface.

It is used to store multiple elements in a linked structure (nodes).

Unlike ArrayList, elements are not stored in continuous memory locations.

Why do we use LinkedList?

We use LinkedList when we frequently:

Add elements
Remove elements
Insert elements in the middle

Because these operations are faster than ArrayList.
example
Imagine a train.

Engine ⇄ Coach1 ⇄ Coach2 ⇄ Coach3

Each coach is connected to the next coach.

If you want to add a new coach:

Engine ⇄ Coach1 ⇄ New Coach ⇄ Coach2 ⇄ Coach3

Just connect the links.

This is how a LinkedList work
Syntax
LinkedList<String> list = new LinkedList<>();
Simple Example
import java.util.LinkedList;

public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        LinkedList<String> list = new LinkedList<>();

        list.add("Apple");
        list.add("Orange");
        list.add("Mango");

        list.addFirst("Banana");

        list.addLast("Grapes");

        System.out.println(list);

        list.removeFirst();

        list.removeLast();

        System.out.println(list);
    }
}
output

[Banana, Apple, Orange, Mango, Grapes]

[Apple, Orange, Mango



